## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/smoothfill.html
- Summary (EN): Smooth Fill fills a region of a layer with smoothly varying values. It solves the Poisson equation inside the provided fill area, so the filled region blends into the boundary values around it.
- Résumé (FR) : Smooth Fill remplit une zone d'un calque avec des valeurs qui varient en douceur, en résolvant l'équation de Poisson à l'intérieur de la zone de remplissage.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer to fill", "fillarea: Mono layer defining which pixels get filled", "mask (optional): per-pixel amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type the source accepts", "Mask: mix between original and new value, default 1 uses only the new value", "Fill: fill pixels Below Threshold or Above Threshold in fillarea", "Threshold: fillarea value where filling starts (dropper can sample it)", "Iterations: relaxation passes used to smooth the filled values", "Acceleration: successive over-relaxation factor, 1 is smooth and stable, up to 1.98 converges faster"]

- Caveats: ["Iterative, may need many iterations to converge", "If not converged, the result depends on resolution", "Starting values close to the final result speed up convergence"]

